    mutex pinned before first backup, held to exit — CodeRabbit r66-#5;
    N8/N9 gates wired). NEW V3-46 (worker-pool.js absence — the zip-overlay
    upload channel cannot delete files, so the round-66 deletion never
    landed remotely; the gap is now sentinel-visible) and V3-47 (.gitignore
    presence + never-commit exclusions — the round-66 zip carried it, the
    bot commit did not).
  - verifier/runs/r67-bench.js (NEW, GPL v3): adversarial benchmark gate
    (N8) — extracts the SHIPPED splitter/scanner implementations from the
    tree, re-checks the isomorphic-twin invariant at runtime, and fails when
    any adversarial case exceeds the 1000ms bound (worst round-67 sandbox
    case 294ms; the round-66 forms cost minutes at these input sizes).
    Linearity is a behavioral property — this harness makes the bound
    executable, the v3 text predicates are tripwires against the known-bad
    forms only.
  - verifier/runs/r62-negative-tests.sh (GPL v3): flock workspace mutex
    (T10) taken before the first backup and held to process exit so every
    trap-path restore runs under the lock; NEW N8 (benchmark gate) and N9
    (concurrency negative: a second instance must fail fast non-zero with
    the lock message and zero tree contact).
